# API Controller Conventions

## BaseController Pattern

All controllers inherit `BaseController` (not `ControllerBase` directly).

```csharp
public class ExpenseController : BaseController
{
    // Use CurrentUserId and IsAdmin — never parse UserId from body
    var result = await _service.GetAllAsync(CurrentUserId, filters);
}
```

## HTTP Conventions

- `ActionResult<T>` when returning data; `IActionResult` for void (Delete)
- POST create → `201 Created`; DELETE → `204 NoContent`
- CSV export → `return File(bytes, "text/csv", "expenses.csv")`
- Auth endpoints (`AuthController`) are public — no `[Authorize]`
- Admin-only: `[Authorize(Roles = "Admin")]`

## Middleware Pipeline Order (do not change)

```
GlobalExceptionMiddleware → HttpsRedirection → CORS → Authentication → Authorization → Swagger → MapControllers
```

## Configuration

- JWT secret only in `appsettings.Development.json` (gitignored)
- CORS origins from `Cors:AllowedOrigins` config — never hardcoded
- Namespace: `ExpenseManager.API.Controllers`

## Authorization Rules

- Users access only their own expenses/categories
- Predefined categories readable by everyone
- Admin manages users (list all, get by id with admin check)
- Ownership validated in service layer, not just controller
